0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (The sharpest economics trap belongs to the rep, not the merchant. James Shepherd of CCSalesPro tells) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (reps to reclassify cash discounting as flat-rate pricing, because what they actually earn is the service fee) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (collected on card transactions, and flat rate behaves nothing like interchange plus. The sweet spot is a $25) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (to $70 average ticket, where signature debit at 22 cents plus 5 basis points lands around 30 to 32 cents) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (all-in, roughly 1% of a $30 sale, leaving about 180 basis points of markup on a 3% fee [AnhJYbY3ptw @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (00:01:30]. Below that band the math flips. A $10 average ticket makes 32 cents equal 3.2%, so a 3% fee) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (puts residuals at negative 20 basis points, and a $5 ticket costs 6.4%, still underwater at 3.99%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm ([AnhJYbY3ptw @ 00:02:44]. The other edge is high ticket: a $150 average jewelry store or a B2B account) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (swiping corporate reward cards with 2.5% interchange earns almost nothing on a 3% fee [AnhJYbY3ptw @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (00:04:12]. That is the check to run before copying a blanket offer like Titan Merchant Services' three to four) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (percent cash discount pitched to businesses from all different industry types [lsC_M7zjTjY @ 00:01:26].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (Shepherd's fixes are a per-item fee such as 59 cents on tiny tickets and a higher percentage on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (rewards-heavy high-ticket books.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (On the street, the deal usually dies on wording, not math. Joe Wagner is blunt that walking in and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (announcing the merchant can drop their fees by charging their customers does not work, because the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (merchant has not yet been made to feel the savings or remember being the consumer [KRZuPsngOLw @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (00:03:12]. The second killer is the awkward pause. Reps who pitch without the application already on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (table eventually run out of things to say, then reach for the app and trigger a rapid-fire list of reasons not to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (sign today; Wagner keeps the app out from the first bridge so the paperwork never arrives as a threat) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm ([tgxPcd70hpA @ 00:19:42]. The third is over-talking after the yes. Once the rep is asking for address and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (phone number, Wagner says deals are so fragile that one unnecessary detail can trigger ten more rebuttals,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (and Wagner fully expects reps who ignore this to call after walking out without the deal [tgxPcd70hpA @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (00:24:41]. Shepherd reports a personal reversal: the old pitch opened with eliminating fees to spark) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (curiosity, then rural Pennsylvania showed those hoops could be skipped in favor of leading straight with the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (fuel station question, now threaded through the opening, the objection preamble and the rebuttal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm ([3bPRCy508Lc @ 00:05:20].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (Structural traps sit underneath the pitch. Shepherd moved reps off the non-cash adjustment because that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (program was clearly under attack by the card brands, with Visa coming out strongly against a fee line item) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (on the receipt [3bPRCy508Lc @ 00:02:08]. FTx POS flags the surcharge trap from the other side: over 80%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (of card transactions in its parent company stores would be flagged as debit and could not be surcharged at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (all, and surcharging is also not available for all Amex cards, capped at 3% or actual cost, live in only 47) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (states, with seven more states carrying pending legislation to ban it [YyYXmSsR5as @ 00:00:58]. Platform) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (choice can block the whole program: Chad The POS Guy says Toast and Square cannot pass the fee to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.57 Tm (customer, so a merchant doing $30,000 a month at about 3% eats $900 out of pocket and takes home) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.35 Tm (roughly $29,100 [pNxf7ZuEt5w @ 00:00:48]. PaymentCloud adds the leftover-cost check: some processors) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 183.12 Tm (still charge small transaction or service fees even under dual pricing, so every cost line needs review before) Tj ET
