BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (support, calls roughly 50% the current industry average, and says 70% or 80% splits usually come with no) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (up-front bonus [ruAqtp4NcPA @ 00:03:32]. Shepard will still take 30% or 40% if that processor hands over) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (leads and coaching that produce far more sales. Shepard also warns that an 80% split stacked with an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (up-front bonus usually means the Schedule A cost was raised, a big piece of a smaller pie [ruAqtp4NcPA @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (00:04:41]. Joe Wagner pushes harder against headline numbers: a company can promise 70%, 80%, even) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (100%, but 100% of something you do not control and are not protected on is not the deal it looks like) Tj ET
