BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (with as a processor matters more for your bottom line than any percentage split, because reps who quietly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (built six-figure residuals chose their processor carefully [AdPAOJ52cvk @ 00:00:20]. The working read:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (Shepard weighs the split against leads and Schedule A cost, Wagner weighs it against contract durability,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (and Gaye weighs it against how the processor treats merchants after the signature.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (The second fault line is front money versus back-end residual. Rich Norton, speaking on CCSalesPro, runs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (Payrock programs paying 250 up front for traditional processing, 500 for the choice programs, plus 150 from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (the leasing company on top, and says reps writing two or three merchants a week make a couple thousand) Tj ET
