BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (calling lease-heavy processors quick money now and very little later because the residual percentage is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (very low, and it lets reps give away terminals only by deducting the cost from their own residuals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm ([Fc87Q5Igrbc @ 00:01:10]. Joe Wagner splits the difference by treating the up-front commission as getting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (paid to acquire an asset that behaves like a rental property, with time as the only investment [6Gf0BTz5h5E) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (@ 00:05:40]. Norton's camp says the up-front check is what keeps a new rep from delivering pizzas at night,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (while Electronic Money Company insists the real money is in the residual income.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (Pricing and prospecting playbooks also diverge. Gaye says dual pricing pays agents the highest residual) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (commission, yet some processors only allow dual pricing, which forces a rep to walk away from any) Tj ET
