BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 693.77 Tm (The hardest economics check comes from Finance Blueprint's ISO model. On a $100 card sale the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 678.55 Tm (merchant pays $2.61 and the company's markup is 45 cents, but after 13 cents of processor and acquiring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (cost only 32 cents is retained; hand a 30% residual to the agent and roughly 22.4 cents is left before support) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (and risk costs [_wQk1Avcku8 @ 00:06:22]. Scale does not rescue that margin quickly. Operating losses run) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (through year four and push peak modeled cash use to about $15.86 million, including the original) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (investment, against a launch budget of only $4 million [_wQk1Avcku8 @ 00:21:07]. Year five finally handles) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (nearly $5.6 billion in payments and bills nearly $150 million in gross card fees, yet recognizes only about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm ($20.7 million in net revenue and produces about $1.63 million in EBITDA; the layers between those) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (numbers are the business [_wQk1Avcku8 @ 00:19:46]. nexio's wholesale breakdown lands on the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (economics gate from the software side: registration only pays once processing revenue exceeds application,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (legal, underwriting, PCI and integration costs, which usually means a large established client base already) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (generating significant transaction volume [wCnscoBFCKc @ 00:05:12]. Run your own merchant book) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (through those same layers before walking away from a working agent deal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (Retention is where portfolios quietly bleed. Finance Blueprint models 1.2% monthly merchant churn, roughly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (13.5% a year, and lists the triggers: a restaurant switching after a terminal outage during a busy shift, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (retailer leaving over a confusing statement, an online merchant moving after a gateway integration fails) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm ([_wQk1Avcku8 @ 00:14:51]. County Portal puts the same trap in street terms: when a client's terminal goes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (down on a busy Friday night, you are the person they call, and fast support is how you keep merchants for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (the long haul [QZSSbXV33jg @ 00:02:30]. Shepherd learned the outsourcing version of that pain firsthand,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (because anything sent to the upstream full service provider came back unbranded, so merchants calling) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (customer service heard another company's name and asked why underwriting ran through someone else) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm ([-sMJDgFoiSM @ 00:00:58]. Sponsor dependency sits underneath all of it. Finance Blueprint flags it as one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (of the largest risks: the bank or acquiring partner can change requirements, pricing, reserve demands or risk) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (appetite, and if the relationship ends, moving merchants elsewhere may be difficult and is never assured) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm ([_wQk1Avcku8 @ 00:22:14]. Every merchant that walks takes its residual with it, so service capacity has to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (be budgeted before growth, not after.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (On the sales floor, the traps come down to pipeline and people. Craig of Merchant Service Slayers says) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (telemarketing-booked appointments close only five to ten percent for a new rep against twenty to thirty) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (percent for a seasoned closer who can get around the through-the-door objections, and that online funnel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (leads close higher but cost more, so the lead promises you make to recruits have to stay brutally real) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm ([pHeumyF-Dw4 @ 00:02:06]. Training is the next leak: Craig warns against teaching new hires a pile of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (elaborate [expletive] they cannot retain before the basics stick, comparing it to dragging a newborn on a ten) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (mile hike, and recommends building reps from crawl to walk to run [pHeumyF-Dw4 @ 00:04:03]. Rich flags) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (the boarding wall: an ISO simply cannot sell if the processor rejects 40% of the applications it submits as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (high risk or niche, which is why underwriting flexibility and multiple bank relationships sit on the scorecard) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm ([kpo2g7o_Ylg @ 00:02:29]. Natalie of DepositFix names the rate-war trap: agents piled onto restaurants,) Tj ET
