BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 462.55 Tm (sales start coming in and the payment account gets frozen with 90 days of revenue locked inside, a pattern) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 447.32 Tm (common for supplement, skin care, CBD and subscription brands [-G2UpQAf8L0 @ 00:00:00]. Because) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 432.10 Tm (Stripe and PayPal bundle the gateway and the merchant account, one decision from them can shut down) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 416.87 Tm (everything at once, and jumping 10 times your volume overnight is a great way to get noticed [-G2UpQAf8L0) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 401.65 Tm (@ 00:06:03]. A high-risk account is not a free pass either; Funnelish warns you can still lose it if) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 386.42 Tm (chargebacks climb too high. The thresholds are lower than most operators assume. Scott E. Adams says a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 371.20 Tm (monitoring-program notice can trigger at over 100 chargebacks combined with a ratio generally over 0.9) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 355.97 Tm (percent, and that merchants with no real relationship with their bank often have no idea what to do when it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 340.75 Tm (lands [gROmfVmEsYs @ 00:00:55]. Adaptiv Payments adds that excessive chargebacks is a reason code) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 325.52 Tm (for the MATCH list, and that most banks step in well before the network limits, so the target is to stay far) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 310.30 Tm (under them, not just under the line [NdTgGwtE_N4 @ 00:01:29].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 295.07 Tm (The second cluster of losses comes from data the merchant never sees. Adaptiv Payments flags the detail) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 279.85 Tm (most merchants miss: once a bank logs a fraud report, it counts toward Visa's ratio even if you refund the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 264.62 Tm (order later, so fraud has to be stopped before you ship [NdTgGwtE_N4 @ 00:02:37]. Adams explains why) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 249.40 Tm (that bites low-ticket sellers hardest: issuers often flag a cheap transaction as fraud without bothering to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 234.17 Tm (charge it back, and that flag still goes against you in Visa's fraud monitoring, so watching chargebacks alone) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 218.95 Tm (leaves you blind and the TC40 file becomes critical [gJ_2exzq6FA @ 00:01:17]. RDR carries its own) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 203.72 Tm (reporting trap. The refund is pulled by the acquirer and marked with what Adams believes is an M flag, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 188.50 Tm (processors, ISOs and gateways further down the chain often never get that change, see a chargeback, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 173.27 Tm (treat it as one, so you have to track it really carefully; RDR also does nothing to keep you out of the fraud) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 158.05 Tm (program [5mi35dvcRrA @ 00:04:08]. Alerts, by contrast, more often clear both the fraud flag and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 142.82 Tm (chargeback, and Adams reports good luck getting clients out of monitoring programs with alerts and RDR in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 127.60 Tm (combination [5mi35dvcRrA @ 00:05:19].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 112.37 Tm (The last set of traps is operational and shows up directly in the margin. Chargeback.io warns that without a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 97.15 Tm (gateway integration, Ethoca and CDRN alerts cannot be matched to the transaction, so you manually locate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 81.92 Tm (and refund every single alert, while only RDR refunds automatically without integration [sH9CslJpDeA @) Tj ET
